        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.701,
            0.743,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": "z Why is it possible to pile up stones or sand, but not a liquid like water?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.744,
            0.743,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": "z Why does water take the shape of folded hands but lose that shape when released?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.786,
            0.743,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": "z We cannot see air, so how does it add weight to an inflated balloon?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.829,
            0.574,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": "z Is the air we breathe today the same that existed thousands of years ago?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.872,
            0.342,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "z Share your questions"
